<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tasker H. Bliss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tasker H. Bliss (1853–1930) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army general who governed the Moro Province in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1906 to 1909. He later served as Chief of Staff of the Army in 1917 and as American military representative on the Supreme War Council in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and was a delegate to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-conference-1919-1920">Paris Peace Conference</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tasker-h-bliss.jpg" alt="Tasker H. Bliss" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:111-SC-12011_-_NARA_-_55184147_(cropped)_(cropped)_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
